# Active Verification — MVP Implementation Plan

**Goal:** Build a working, end-to-end Minimum Viable Pipeline that takes a suspicious email, scores it, investigates the sender domain, runs a sandboxed honeypot simulation, and displays all evidence on a dashboard.

---

## Architecture Overview

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "Frontend"
        D["Streamlit Dashboard<br/>(port 8501)"]
    end
    subgraph "Backend (FastAPI, port 8000)"
        A["POST /detect"]
        B["POST /investigate"]
        C["POST /unmask"]
        E["GET /pipeline/{id}"]
    end
    subgraph "Database"
        F["PostgreSQL<br/>(port 5432)"]
    end

    D -->|HTTP calls| A
    D -->|HTTP calls| B
    D -->|HTTP calls| C
    D -->|HTTP calls| E
    A --> F
    B --> F
    C --> F
```

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Frontend Choice: Streamlit over React.** Since the MVP goal is speed-to-working and your team is Python-focused, I recommend **Streamlit** for the dashboard. It requires zero JavaScript/HTML knowledge, can call FastAPI endpoints via `httpx`, and gets a functional UI in hours rather than days. The trade-off is limited customization — but for a capstone demo, it's ideal. React can be swapped in later if needed. **Do you agree?**

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Model Choice: DistilBERT instead of DeBERTa-v3-base for MVP.** DeBERTa-v3-base is excellent but heavy (~440MB, slow on CPU). For the MVP to run on any laptop without a GPU, I recommend starting with **DistilBERT** (~260MB, 2× faster inference). We can upgrade to DeBERTa later once the pipeline works. The training code is identical — just swap the model name. **Your preference?**

> [!WARNING]
> **LLM for Investigation Agent.** The Investigate module needs an LLM to reason about WHOIS/DNS evidence. Options:
> 1. **OpenAI API** (GPT-4o-mini) — easiest, costs ~$0.15/1M tokens, requires API key
> 2. **Google Gemini API** (gemini-1.5-flash) — free tier available, requires API key
> 3. **Ollama (local)** — fully free, requires ~4GB RAM for a 7B model, no API key
>
> I recommend **Option 2 (Gemini Flash)** for the MVP since it's free and you've used Google APIs before. We'll make it configurable so any provider works. **Which do you prefer?**

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> 1. **Do you already have Docker Desktop installed on Windows?** The Docker Compose setup requires it.
